Original commit body from a7a9aaeaae82e2c174f172297a879df041e46631:

Core-linker half of WI-pivap (mechanism B). _create_inheritance_edges
retried a qualified base's last segment with no qualifier check, so C#
System.Exception, C++ std::exception, Go io.Writer and Java
java.util.ArrayList<String> bound any in-repo class of that name.

- _qualifier_fit: the last segment binds only candidates whose
  qualified_name fits the written base (either ends with the other on a
  segment boundary: producers disagree on what qualified_name holds;
  C#/Java/Kotlin/Go/C++ include the namespace, Python the in-module
  qualname). Candidates with no qualified_name keep the name binding.
  When every candidate records one and none fits, the base is external
  (_qualified_external_edge, the written qualifier as its module).
- cpp: class and struct symbols record their namespace-qualified name.

Not handled: a BARE base imported through a namespace import (C# using,
PHP use, Groovy / Scala imports) -- needs import context the linker lacks.

